               <head>Documents relating to Romney Marsh, etc., c. 1361-1481; England, late 15th century</head>
               <msContents>
                  <!--<msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_Gough_Kent_27-item1">
                     <title key="work_11654">Documents relating to , 1340 and later</title>
                     
                     
                     <!-\- ordinances pursuant to sewer commission of 3 Aug. 14 Edw [IV?] (1474?) - cf Dugdale, Imbanking, 48 for a similar commission of this year -\->
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>-->
                  <!--</msItem>-->
                  <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_Gough_Kent_27-item1">
                     <locus>(fols. 7r-8v)</locus>
                     <rubric>Commissio justiciis ad sewaras</rubric>
                     <note>Commission of Edward IV of sewers (<foreign>de walliis et fossatis</foreign>) to Edward Nevylle of Bergevenny et al. 'super costeram marisci Thamis a villa de Westgrenewich ... vsque Gravesende', 3 August 1474 [<title>Calendar of Patent Rolls 1467-1477</title>, p. 463; W. Dugdale, <title>History of Imbanking ...</title> (1662), p. 62], including the power to make statutes and ordinances for those parts according to the law and custom of <placeName key="place_4009399">Romney Marsh</placeName>.</note>
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem n="2" xml:id="MS_Gough_Kent_27-item2">
                     <locus>(fols. 8v-12r)</locus>
                     <title type="desc">Ordinances of Thomas Ludlow and others for <placeName key="place_4009399">Romney Marsh</placeName> [1361 (?)]</title>
                     <note>The text follows on directly from the preceding document.</note>
                     <incipit>Per quod mandatum ijdem Thomas Robertus et Thomas</incipit>
                     <explicit>siue in comitatu Kanc' siue in comitatu Sussex'.</explicit>
                     <listBibl>
                        <bibl>M. Teichman Derville, <title>The Level and the Liberty of Romney Marsh ...</title> (Ashford, Kent, 1936), pp. 14-16</bibl>
                        <bibl>English summary in Dugdale, <title>Imbanking</title>, 31-33; E. Turner, 'The statutes of the marshes of Pevensey and Romney ...', <title>Sussex Archaelogical Collections</title> 18 (1866), 42-53 at <ref target="https://archive.org/details/sussexarchaeolog18suss_0/page/48/mode/2up">pp. 47-49</ref> summarizes a Middle English version in MS. Dugdale 43.</bibl></listBibl>
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem n="3" xml:id="MS_Gough_Kent_27-item3">
                     <locus>(fols. 12r-18r)</locus>
                     <title type="desc">Ordinances for 'Est Malham' marsh established by Richard Wakhurst and others, [1440 (?)]</title>
                     <note>Pursuant to letters patent of Henry VI referring to the parliament of 18 Henry VI [?= <title>Calendar of Patent Rolls </title>, p. 372 (Dugdale, <title>Imbanking</title>, p. 47), dated 12 March 1440 and referring to the parishes of Tenterden and Rolvenden]</note>
                     <note>The final clause is in English and breaks off unfinished at the end of fol. 18r 'or the lande with the choyse by þe'. Marginal note, fol. 12r, 'et cum hoc concordant statuta marisci de Wallond' [Welland].</note>
                     <textLang mainLang="la" otherLangs="enm">Latin and Middle English</textLang>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem n="4" xml:id="MS_Gough_Kent_27-item4">
                     <locus>(fol. 18v)</locus>
                     <rubric>Modus <sic>tenenendi</sic> curiam vocatam le Lathe in marisco</rubric>
                     <note>Form for proceedings of a last or lathe court (cf. Teichman Derville, ch. 2), dated 3 October 21 Edw. IV (1481)</note>
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  </msItem>
                  <msItem n="5" xml:id="MS_Gough_Kent_27-item5">
                     <locus>(fol. 19r)</locus>
                     <title type="desc">Form documents: receipts for 'waterskotte' delivered by a collector in 'the parts of Kent or Sussex' to the bailiff or 'expenditor' of the marsh of 'P.'</title>
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  </msItem>
